WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.721 --> 00:00:16.326
Gildong the Hwalbindang were in a village by the sea.

2
00:00:17.287 --> 00:00:18.747
They were handing out grain.

3
00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:25.710
A sign caught Gildong's eye.

4
00:00:30.861 --> 00:00:32.041
He laughed as he read it.

5
00:00:32.061 --> 00:00:33.742
"What's so funny?"

6
00:00:34.222 --> 00:00:34.983
Nabi asked.

7
00:00:35.003 --> 00:00:39.105
"I'm the new minister of war," Gildong said.

8
00:00:39.125 --> 00:00:41.987
"The king is ordering me to come to the palace."

9
00:00:43.908 --> 00:00:45.289
Mok scratched his head.

10
00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:47.230
"Why is that funny?"

11
00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:51.352
"The king's still trying to capture me," Gildong said.

12
00:00:51.372 --> 00:00:53.353
"I guess he'll never give up."

13
00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.775
"What will you do?"

14
00:00:57.295 --> 00:00:58.236
Chibong asked.

15
00:01:01.784 --> 00:01:03.845
Gildong looked out across the sea.

16
00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.606
"I think it's time for a new adventure.

17
00:01:07.506 --> 00:01:09.407
But first I am going to the palace."

18
00:01:09.427 --> 00:01:13.289
"What?" Mok gulped.

19
00:01:13.309 --> 00:01:15.630
"You can't go, boss.

20
00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:16.930
It's not safe."

21
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.652
"I'll be fine," Gildong said.

22
00:01:20.672 --> 00:01:23.953
"I must see the king and end this once and for all."

23
00:01:28.635 --> 00:01:30.196
He gathered everyone closer.

24
00:01:33.048 --> 00:01:46.674
"Here is what you must do while I'm gone At the palace Gildong entered the courtyard.

25
00:01:46.694 --> 00:01:49.095
"Your Majesty."

26
00:01:52.576 --> 00:01:53.617
Gildong bowed.

27
00:01:53.637 --> 00:01:59.079
"I am lowborn, yet you want me as your minister of war.

28
00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:00.520
I'm honored."

29
00:02:02.272 --> 00:02:03.133
Heup grinned.

30
00:02:03.153 --> 00:02:05.714
"Now!" he yelled.

31
00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:09.877
Soldiers ran in and surrounded Gildong.

32
00:02:11.458 --> 00:02:13.399
Their spears moved in fast.

33
00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.621
But Gildong reached for his fan.

34
00:02:16.641 --> 00:02:23.225
"Fly!" did he go?"

35
00:02:23.545 --> 00:02:24.406
the king cried.

36
00:02:25.867 --> 00:02:27.808
Gildong stood high above.

37
00:02:30.104 --> 00:02:32.685
He laughed as everyone below looked for him.

38
00:02:32.705 --> 00:02:34.306
"Up here!"

39
00:02:36.266 --> 00:02:37.407
The crowd looked up.

40
00:02:37.427 --> 00:02:42.628
"Your Majesty is very generous to make me a minister," Gildong said.

41
00:02:42.648 --> 00:02:44.949
"But I'm going to refuse the position.

42
00:02:45.649 --> 00:02:46.869
You'll be rid of me at last."

43
00:02:46.889 --> 00:02:51.651
"What?" The king looked shocked.

44
00:02:52.971 --> 00:02:56.152
"I'm leaving your kingdom for a new adventure," Gildong said.

45
00:02:57.472 --> 00:03:00.414
"I'll create a new country with the Hwalbindang, far from here.

46
00:03:01.494 --> 00:03:03.175
Lowborn people will be treated fairly.

47
00:03:03.896 --> 00:03:06.037
They will have the same opportunities as nobles.

48
00:03:10.199 --> 00:03:16.723
Good-bye." Gildong opened his fan, and a fierce wind swirled around the palace.

49
00:03:21.586 --> 00:03:23.727
He soared high into the sky.

50
00:03:29.496 --> 00:03:31.598
Thwoosh! He landed on a large ship.

51
00:03:35.061 --> 00:03:36.302
Chibong hurried over.

52
00:03:36.322 --> 00:03:40.105
"Everything's ready, boss, just as you requested."

53
00:03:40.125 --> 00:03:43.708
"Are we really leaving, little lord?"

54
00:03:44.168 --> 00:03:44.949
Nabi asked.

55
00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:46.931
Gildong sighed.

56
00:03:46.951 --> 00:03:49.413
"I'm not a lord."

57
00:03:49.433 --> 00:03:53.156
"But you are our boss."

58
00:03:54.457 --> 00:03:55.358
Mok laughed.

59
00:03:55.378 --> 00:03:57.760
"Maybe you should be our king!"

60
00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:00.901
Gildong shook his head.

61
00:04:00.921 --> 00:04:02.462
"I don't think so.

62
00:04:03.203 --> 00:04:04.543
I only want to do good in the world.

63
00:04:05.584 --> 00:04:06.285
Now let's go!"

64
00:04:11.788 --> 00:04:14.050
Everyone sang as the ship took off.

65
00:04:16.131 --> 00:04:18.072
"We'll sail to a new land.

66
00:04:18.473 --> 00:04:20.394
We'll make everything grand.

67
00:04:20.774 --> 00:04:24.417
Thanks to Hong Gildong."

68
00:04:26.118 --> 00:04:29.020
The Hwalbindang sailed beyond the horizon.

69
00:04:30.173 --> 00:04:33.043
And only they know what happened next.
